  slide "One fire-and-forget snapshot before the ship" {
    eyebrow: "5 · Heartbeat"
    title: "One fire-and-forget snapshot before the ship"
    lede: "Each cell ships exactly one MetricsHeartbeat, fire-and-forget with no reply, immediately before its terminal partition. The snapshot carries counters, mergeable sketches, and an observation time, so the controller can merge every cell's final numbers into a live cross-cell view as each cell finishes."
    narration: "Each cell ships one fire-and-forget heartbeat right before its terminal partition. The controller merges every cell's counters and sketches into a live cross-cell view as each cell finishes; a cell that never ships within the deadline makes the controller abort loudly."
    term: {
      word: "MetricsHeartbeat"
      meaning: "One-shot cell→controller snapshot of counts and sketches, sent immediately before the terminal partition; the controller merges every cell's heartbeat into a live cross-cell aggregate for the report sidecar."
    }
    points: [
      "Fire-and-forget: the heartbeat never blocks on a reply, off the per-request hot path.",
      "Blocking by design — called once, right before the terminal partition ship.",
      "Evidence: `rust/runtime/src/cellular/heartbeat.rs`, `engine/cellular_controller.rs`."
    ]
    caption: "one snapshot, shipped once → live cross-cell aggregate."

    render: @scene {
      sdk.Header(
        id = "s4-hdr",
